fairpipe keeps a schema-compatible local subset for tests only. It does not vendor
the full BBQ release and does not load that subset by default. Optional
`load_bbq_items(fetch_upstream=True)` pulls from the pinned commit. BBQ categories
reflect U.S. English protected-class context and should not be treated as a global
stereotype taxonomy. `stereotype_association_score` is experimental and is not the
published BBQ bias score (see GitHub issue #31).
